<?xml version="1.0"?>
<CP_Scriptfile date="Feb 20, 2023">
<CPscript title="Discrete Rational Example" level="min" screenmode="map" >
<description>A discrete rational map is a map between a maximal packing of the sphere and a branched packing of the sphere with the same combinatorics. Here we illustrate with an example constructed using Schwarz triangles.</description>
<text> This script illustrates a discrete rational map analogous to the classical rational map F(z)=z^2(z^5-7)/(7z^5+1). It is based on a 42-circle pattern having dodecahedral symmetry. </text>
<cmd name="*" mnemonic="*" iconname="run.png">act 0;Cleanse;Map 0 1;infile_read max.p;color -c 100 a;color -c s0 a(1 12);Disp -w -c </cmd>
<text> The packing has 12 circles of degree 5, the remaining 30 are of degree 6. We color code the degree 5. </text>
<cmd iconname="metacontact_offline.png">Disp -p0 -w -c -cf a(1 12) </cmd>
<text> The next command puts a branched packing with these same combinatorics in p1. It has 12 simple branch points, and valence 7. The branch points, each of degree 5, are color coded to match the colors in p0. Pressing 'b' on one of these colored circles in the domain will display its flower in p0 and its image flower in p1. Note that the 5 neighbors go twice around in the image packing.

The radii and layout of the branched packing cannot be computed by CirclePack. Instead, this packing was created using (2 3 5) Schwarz triangles and their reflective structure. See Section 6.8 and "SoccerPack.xmd". </text>
<cmd iconname="userconfig.png">act 1;infile_read branched.p;color -c 100 a;color -c s0 a(1 12);Disp -w -c -cfn a(1 12) </cmd>
<text> I will leave it to you to investigate this fascinating packing. The keys 'c' and 'f' toggle the display mode between circles and dual faces. </text>
<Section title="Tools">
<cmd inline="no" name="f" mnemonic="f" tooltip="display face mode" iconname="centrejust.png">Disp -p0 -w -dff;Disp -p1 -w -df -dff a(1 12) </cmd>
<cmd inline="no" name="c" mnemonic="c" tooltip="display circle mode" iconname="dnd_multi.png">Disp -p0 -w -c -cf a(1 12);Disp -p1 -w -c -cf a(1 12); </cmd>
<cmd inline="no" name="b" mnemonic="b" tooltip="display a branch points flower" iconname="psi.png">set_Vlist z #XY;set_Flist Iv Vlist;disp -p0 -w -f Flist -cf Vlist -c Iv Vlist;disp -p1 -w -f Flist -cf Vlist -c Iv Vlist </cmd>
</Section>
  </CPscript>
